  "evidence": [
    "Actual PostgreSQL migration, exact anonymous token lookup, company/foreign-account isolation, immutable coordinates, current parent/device/security guards and terminal revision.",
    "Actual encrypted repository creation, refresh lost-response replay, old/current keyring behavior and PostgreSQL archive restoration.",
    "Recovery SQL produces the same authenticated purposes as Kotlin for actual encrypted bootstrap and refresh rows, which decrypt to the exact committed pairs.",
    "Creation, rotation and retirement writes roll back on missing/foreign readback, I/O failure, cancellation, interruption and interrupted thread flags.",
    "Competing actual refreshes retain one winner; the original refresh recovers only that committed pair.",
    "Expired cleanup skips a locked row, remains bounded, and preserves owned metadata/token facts after native purge and offboarding.",
    "Malformed raw metadata, scope/hash substitution, legacy-purpose substitution, immutable deadlines/parent and exact readback are checked inside repository failure boundaries."
